course: dictionary
lesson: 9426
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Stab» is a good example. A grey heron may stab a fish, and you may have a stab at an answer. The sentence shows you which meaning to use.
explain: Look at the words near the word. «A stab of pain» is a sudden sharp feeling, not a knife at all. «Have a stab at the answer» means try your best guess. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Some phrases have a meaning that is different from the single words in them. «Stab in the back» does not mean hurting someone's body. In a story it means a betrayal, when a friend secretly does something hurtful to you. Phrases like this are best learned as a group.
fact: To stab means to push a knife or another sharp, pointed thing into someone or something.
fact: To stab can also mean to push or poke something hard with a pointed object or finger.
fact: A stab is a sudden sharp pain or feeling, as in «a stab of pain» or «a stab of jealousy».
fact: To have a stab at something means to try it, as in «Have a stab at the answer».
fact: Carrying knives is against the law and dangerous, and stabbing someone is a serious crime.
exercise: «He felt a stab of pain in his foot.» What does stab mean here? | A cut made with a knife | A loud noise | A long, slow ache | *A sudden sharp pain
exercise: Maya says, «Have a stab at the answer.» What does have a stab mean? | To wave your hand in the air | *To try it | To give up and go home | To carry a knife
exercise: «Grey herons stand still in shallow water, then stab with a sudden strike.» What is the heron doing? | *Striking quickly with its beak to catch a fish | Sleeping in the reeds | Swimming in deep water | Calling to its friends
test: «She gave the potato a stab with a fork to check if it was soft.» What does stab mean here? | To peel the skin away | *To push or poke it with a pointed object | To cook it in a pan of oil | To wash the potato under a tap
test: In a story, what does a «stab in the back» mean? | A small cut on the finger | *A betrayal by a friend | A real injury from a fall | A loud shout across the playground
exam: «The bad news came as a stab of sadness.» What does stab mean here? | A slow, quiet walk | A pointed tool for sewing | *A sudden sharp feeling | A kind of cloud
